407:- **Item 4 (exact Docling-Graph implementation and release/commit) — answered for the synthetic development scope.** `docling-project/docling-graph` 1.9.1 and Docling 2.126.0 are locked, with the Graph wheel digest recorded. Native/scanned conversion, saved-JSON reuse, publication before extraction, PostgreSQL recovery, and a recorded-response direct/dense comparison have bounded proof; see [F0005 compatibility evidence](features/archive/F0005-one-time-docling-ingestion/compatibility-evidence.md). F0001's unsuccessful reuse attempt and direct-vLLM results remain historical evidence; its blanket no-reuse conclusion was too broad. Live-model and deployment qualification and reviewer acceptance remain pending under ADR-0060. Requirements/thresholds approved in F0005 plan run `2026-10-23-9a04b327` remain unchanged; Phase B rework `2026-10-25-50fcf658` was approved by the operator on 2026-10-25 after review `2026-10-24-0fbc1de1`. It specifies supervised conversion with a parent-owned 300-second deadline, a host singleton with confirmed provider recovery, and explicit direct-baseline rejection settings. These are planned controls, not runtime proof or activation.
