461:### 4.12 F0006 Phase B design (approved 2026-11-01; implementation pending)
463:[Assembly plan](features/F0006-assertion-plane-origin-and-interpretation-basis/feature-assembly-plan.md), plan run `2026-11-01-7d6d19ce`: Phase A and Phase B approved by operator tokens `approve-phase-a` and `approve-phase-b`; five unstarted stories and 35 ACs. Proposed [ADR-0075](architecture/decisions/ADR-0075-versioned-assertion-semantics-and-admission.md) defines additive typed/open assertion semantics, document-local references/name admission claims, structural quote/name/time checks and eligibility guards at existing review/commit consumers. The legacy strict result contract and source history remain; new schemas are `assertion-record-v2`, `interpretation-result-v2` and `assertion-admission-result-v1`. Case/spacing normalization is deterministic with original-range mapping; repeated text never justifies a fabricated span.
465:No new deployable, assertion HTTP route, UI, grants or extraction activation. Current authorization's mutation facade gains optional source READ requirements in the same unit of work; it must not nest a read facade that commits the outer transaction. Existing `direct-baseline` and v1 content writer defaults follow F0005's final approved rejection decision. Full durable drops/run adoption stays F0016; full source-completeness/commit orchestration stays F0018; display stays F0022; open extraction/alignment stays F0066. New restrictions apply to attributable v2 evidence/review/correction lineage; unregistered legacy pilot references remain an explicit compatibility boundary. ADR-0065 and ADR-0075 remain Proposed until their required runtime proofs. Existing C4 topology is unchanged; feature README contains ER/component diagrams. Phase B design is approved; implementation and required runtime proofs remain pending.
486:Current position (2026-10-25): F0001 to F0004 are done and archived. F0005's synthetic Docling-Graph proof is complete; its unchanged local-qualification requirements/thresholds were approved in plan run `2026-10-23-9a04b327`. Three high plan-review gaps prompted Phase B rework `2026-10-25-50fcf658`, approved by the operator on 2026-10-25 and ready for the feature action (section 4.8); the amendment has its own explicit approval. F0012, F0013 and F0015 carry planning prerequisites and teaching examples but no PRD or approved plan; F0065's stories and draft contracts await review. The roadmap's Now lane is empty: choosing the next feature is an operator decision.
